  "body": "This listing is for the sale of a 798m2 rear freehold site, having a common concrete driveway (¼ share in Lot 27). \r\n\r\nIt enjoys a sunny northerly aspect and limited sea views over Whale Cove to Kawau Island. \r\n\r\nA pedestrian accessway to the clifftop runs down the eastern boundary to Whale Cove.\r\n\r\nG J Gardner has designed a home to show what can be built on the section.  Link to their listing: \r\nhttps://www.trademe.co.nz/a/property/new-homes/house-land/auckland/rodney/red-beach/listing/5755741377\r\n\r\nInterests of note:\r\nTransfer B740599.2 prohibits sheds, commercial use and second-hand dwellings. \r\nTransfer 5890721.1 refers to a height restriction 26.43 metres from origin levels RM5254 SO55541, RL53.735 and \r\nroof is neutral colour. \r\n   \r\nRED BEACH \r\nThis is a popular residential location which was developed in the 1980’s.  \r\nRed Beach is a beautiful white sandy beach with a Surf Club.  This is a popular beachside area and has a local shopping with cafés, petrol station, hairdresser and florist shops.  Pre-school’s and the primary school in Red Beach are popular.   \r\nOrewa is a commercial area, three kilometres north and offers a great variety of shops including supermarkets, specialty shops, medical centre’s, professional services, restaurants and cafes. \r\nDowntown Auckland City is 35 kilometres south, a 30 minute drive during off-peak traffic hours.\r\nDevelopment of the nearby Silverdale Town Centre has been underway over recent years. \r\nThe Silverdale Centre development, in Silverdale Street has 36 shops (24,000m2 of retail space), including The Warehouse and Countdown, together with 980 on-site carparks. \r\nThe Silverdale Medical and Surgical Centre, Northern Arena Swimming Pool & Gym Complex, and Polarity Plaza (9 shops) opened off Hibiscus Coast Highway. \r\nFurther retail office developments, have opened in nearby locations in Silverdale Street, Wainui Road and Millwater Parkway, including Farmers Silverdale Mall and Rebel Sports.  Further development included The Boulevard Apartments, a three storey apartment building with 48 units.",
